Modifications to deck.gl as redistributed by Zebflow
====================================================

What is here
------------

  0.1/runtime/deckgl.bundle.mjs    an upstream deck.gl build
  0.1/runtime/deckgl.patched.mjs   Zebflow's wrapper, which imports the above

The file named "patched" is a Zebflow wrapper around the bundle, not an edit of
deck.gl's source. It adds layer construction from a declarative spec, tooltip
handling, and instance bookkeeping. deck.gl's own code is imported, not altered.

Hydration adopts the mounted instance (0.1.4)
---------------------------------------------

The runtime mounts a server-rendered `<div data-zeb-lib="deckgl">` from its
`data-config` before the page hydrates, and marks the host patched. The
hydrated DeckMap wrapper then saw that mark in its ref callback and returned
without an instance of its own, so every later `setOptions` — the effect that
runs when `layers` change — was a no-op: a layer built from page state (a
GeoJSON fetched on the client, a highlight that follows a timer) never reached
the deck, while the same state changed the DOM around it. The wrapper now
adopts the instance the runtime left on the host and pushes its current config
into it once. Both copies of the wrapper (DeckMap.tsx and the one inside the
patched runtime) carry the change; the bundle is untouched.

Same release: a `GeoJsonLayer` spec is split into Polygon, Path and point
sub-layers, and those specs copied optional props verbatim — `opacity:
cfg.opacity`, `extruded`, `material` — so an unset one reached deck.gl as an
own `undefined`, which shadows the layer's default. A polygon with
`opacity: undefined` renders nothing, silently. Every sub-layer spec now goes
through `withoutUndefined`, as the icon path already did.

Network behaviour: workers off by default (0.1.3)
-------------------------------------------------

The bundle carries three CDN references, all upstream defaults:

  https://unpkg.com/@loaders.gl/...    worker bundles for binary formats
  https://unpkg.com/webgl-debug@2.0.1  only when WebGL debug mode is enabled
  https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/spectorjs  only when the debug-spectorjs flag is set

The bundle is unmodified; the wrapper closes the first door. Every layer built
through the declarative spec gets `loadOptions: { worker: false }` unless the
spec sets its own, so loaders parse in-thread — no worker bundle is ever
fetched. This matters most for MVT, which the mapserver serves: without it, the
first vector-tile layer on a machine with no network would fail with an unpkg
error nobody can act on. In-thread parsing produces the same result; only very
large tiles pay a main-thread cost, and a spec that wants workers back can say
`loadOptions: { worker: true }` and own the network dependency.

Still open, deliberately:

  - Formats whose decoder is a wasm blob (draco, basis) are not covered by the
    worker switch — the wasm itself is a CDN fetch. No shipped layer uses one.
    A layer that needs them must vendor the wasm first, not discover the
    dependency in the field.
  - webgl-debug and spectorjs load only when their debug flags are set, which
    no Zebflow surface sets.
  - Layers constructed directly from bundle classes (not through the spec)
    keep upstream defaults — the spec path is the supported one.
